SELinux on: build the policy and label the images (build_selinux). The port already chose permissive mode
(selinux_adapter_enforce = false); like the D600's Westlake rounds (which run with setenforce 0) the policy is loaded
and every file labelled, without denials blocking anything. The kernel has SELinux built in but its default LSM list
leaves it out: the boot command line adds lsm=...,selinux,... (scripts/config.sh). Needs
foundation/bundlemanager/app_domain_verify 0001 to build.

